setblock 422 115 -843 lectern[facing=north,has_book=true]{Book:{id:"minecraft:written_book",count:1,components:{"minecraft:written_book_content":{title:"Dragon Balls",author:"the Claude SMP",pages:["Three sets of 7 Dragon Balls, 1 to 7 stars: orange in the Overworld, red in the Nether, purple in the End.\n\nGather one full set to summon a dragon.","Balls hide inside structures: in a room, on a roof or a street of a village, tower, ruin or dungeon. Nether and End balls sit in guarded places full of mobs.\n\nHit one to pick it up.\n\nThe End set sleeps until the End opens.","Carrying rules:\nEach ball slows you 5% (all 7: 35%).\n\nNo chests, ender chests, shulkers, bundles, hoppers or item frames - and you can't wear one.","Die and your balls drop where you fell, never your grave.\n\nLog off and they drop where you stood.\n\nLava or the void sends them flying off again.","A ball never leaves its own world: go through a portal (or /home, /spawn) and it stays behind where you left.","Radars, right here:\nDefault Radar 1000\nNether Radar 5000\nEnd Radar 20000\n\nEach points at the nearest awake ball of its own set, in its own world, even a carried one.","The radar's dot moves in as you get closer: Far, Getting warm, Close, Right here.\n\nSneak + right-click to track the next ball instead of the nearest.","Summoning:\nPlace all 7 of one set within 2 blocks of each other. Hold that set's radar and right-click or hit one.\n\nChoose your dragon. The radar shatters. One dragon at a time.","Shenron grants 1 great wish. From the Nether set he rises as Nuova Shenron.\n\nPorunga grants 3, each about half as strong.\n\nOnly the summoner wishes - everyone reads the answer.","Deeper sets, bigger wishes:\n\nA dragon from the Nether set grants about 1.5x an Overworld one.\n\nFrom the End set, 2x.","Good wishes: real money, gear with max enchants, named pets, XP, a build, server effects, time or weather, a chat title, a villager trade.","Never, curse or not: hurting, robbing or finding another player, fly/op/creative, extra wishes, bans - or anything about the balls themselves.","Too big? The dragon may offer a curse instead: a lasting effect, your named items, or never wishing again. You can say no.","After the wish the set flies off 1000-2000 blocks (Nether: 250-500), always in its own world.\n\nFor 3 Minecraft days they're stone: findable, but the radar's blind and they won't summon."]}}}}
setblock 432 115 -840 lectern[facing=west,has_book=true]{Book:{id:"minecraft:written_book",count:1,components:{"minecraft:written_book_content":{title:"Dragon Balls",author:"the Claude SMP",pages:["Three sets of 7 Dragon Balls, 1 to 7 stars: orange in the Overworld, red in the Nether, purple in the End.\n\nGather one full set to summon a dragon.","Balls hide inside structures: in a room, on a roof or a street of a village, tower, ruin or dungeon. Nether and End balls sit in guarded places full of mobs.\n\nHit one to pick it up.\n\nThe End set sleeps until the End opens.","Carrying rules:\nEach ball slows you 5% (all 7: 35%).\n\nNo chests, ender chests, shulkers, bundles, hoppers or item frames - and you can't wear one.","Die and your balls drop where you fell, never your grave.\n\nLog off and they drop where you stood.\n\nLava or the void sends them flying off again.","A ball never leaves its own world: go through a portal (or /home, /spawn) and it stays behind where you left.","Radars, right here:\nDefault Radar 1000\nNether Radar 5000\nEnd Radar 20000\n\nEach points at the nearest awake ball of its own set, in its own world, even a carried one.","The radar's dot moves in as you get closer: Far, Getting warm, Close, Right here.\n\nSneak + right-click to track the next ball instead of the nearest.","Summoning:\nPlace all 7 of one set within 2 blocks of each other. Hold that set's radar and right-click or hit one.\n\nChoose your dragon. The radar shatters. One dragon at a time.","Shenron grants 1 great wish. From the Nether set he rises as Nuova Shenron.\n\nPorunga grants 3, each about half as strong.\n\nOnly the summoner wishes - everyone reads the answer.","Deeper sets, bigger wishes:\n\nA dragon from the Nether set grants about 1.5x an Overworld one.\n\nFrom the End set, 2x.","Good wishes: real money, gear with max enchants, named pets, XP, a build, server effects, time or weather, a chat title, a villager trade.","Never, curse or not: hurting, robbing or finding another player, fly/op/creative, extra wishes, bans - or anything about the balls themselves.","Too big? The dragon may offer a curse instead: a lasting effect, your named items, or never wishing again. You can say no.","After the wish the set flies off 1000-2000 blocks (Nether: 250-500), always in its own world.\n\nFor 3 Minecraft days they're stone: findable, but the radar's blind and they won't summon."]}}}}
setblock 413 115 -865 lectern[facing=north,has_book=true]{Book:{id:"minecraft:written_book",count:1,components:{"minecraft:written_book_content":{title:"More",author:"the Claude SMP",pages:["Skills level up as you play.\n/skills shows them.\n\n/color\npicks a colour for your name.\n\n/pvp\nturns PvP on or off for you.","Carry mobs:\nsneak + right-click a passive mob with an empty hand. Right-click a block to put it down, sneak + left-click to throw.","When you die your items wait in a grave where you died.\n\nVoice chat works for Java players using the server modpack."]}}}}
setblock 414 115 -865 lectern[facing=north,has_book=true]{Book:{id:"minecraft:written_book",count:1,components:{"minecraft:written_book_content":{title:"Tag game",author:"the Claude SMP",pages:["A game of tag runs all the time. Whoever is IT wears a sheep head.\n\nHit a player to tag them, even with PvP off. No damage is done.","Being IT costs points every minute, and getting tagged costs 10.\nLowest score wins.\n\nIT gets a compass that points at players. Right-click to switch target.","/tag optout\nsits the game out.\n/tag optin\njoins back in.\n\n/tag stats\n/tag top\n/tag who\n/tag board"]}}}}
